    紧 | jǐn | tight; urgent; strict

semantic_boundary_contrasts:
  core_nuance: 不要紧 is an informal spoken consolation expressing that a mishap, injury, or mistake is harmless and trivial.
  contrasts[3]{id,compared_word,pinyin,analysis}:
    1 | 不要紧 vs. 没关系 | méi guānxi | 没关系 is polite social etiquette responding to an apology or thanks ('no problem / you're welcome'), whereas 不要紧 specifically addresses health, danger, or injury ('it's not critical / not dangerous').
    2 | 不要紧 vs. 无所谓 | wúsuǒwèi | 不要紧 is warm and reassuring about low risk, whereas 无所谓 expresses apathy, indifference, or unconcern ('I don't care either way').
    3 | 不要紧 vs. 不碍事 | bú àishì | Both mean not hindering, but 不碍事 emphasizes that something does not physically block an action, while 不要紧 focuses on severity of consequences.

extended_reading_passages[2]{id,hanzi,pinyin,en,es}:
  #1 | 生活中难免会遇到跌倒与挫折，一句温暖从容的“不要紧”，往往胜过千言万语的劝慰。它不仅能抚平内心的慌乱与沮丧，更能给予前行者重整旗鼓的勇气。学会坦然面对得失，人生才能走得更加宽广从容。 | Shēnghuó zhōng nánmiǎn huì yùdào diēdǎo yǔ cuòzhé, yí jù wēnnuǎn cóngróng de 'búyàojǐn', wǎngwǎng shèngguò qiānyán-wànyǔ de quànwèi. Tā bùjǐn néng fǔpíng nèixīn de huāngluàn yǔ jǔsàng, gèng néng jǐyǔ qiánxíngzhě chóngzhěng-qígǔ de yǒngqì. Xuéhuì tǎnrán miànduì déshī, rénshēng cáinéng zǒu de gèngjiā kuānguǎng cóngróng. | Stumbles and setbacks are inevitable in life; a warm, tranquil 'it doesn't matter' often outshines thousands of words. It smooths away panic and confers courage to regroup. Facing gains and losses with equanimity broadens one's path. | Los tropiezos son inevitables en la vida; un apacible 'no pasa nada' vale más que mil consuelos. Calma el desasosiego y alienta a recomponer fuerzas. Mirar con serenidad las vicisitudes ensancha el horizonte vital.
  #2 | 在危机管理与团队决策中，优秀的领导者既能在战略上洞察全局，又能在战术失误时以“不要紧”的豁达胸襟稳定军心。允许团队在试错中探索成长，恰恰是激发组织内部创新活力与坚韧韧性的关键所在。 | Zài wēijī guǎnlǐ yǔ tuánduì juécè zhōng, yōuxiù de lǐngdǎozhě jì néng zài zhànlüè shàng dòngchá quánjú, yòu néng zài zhànshù shīwù shí yǐ 'búyàojǐn' de huòdá xiōngjīn wěndìng jūnxīn. Yǔnxǔ tuánduì zài shìcuò zhōng tànsuǒ chéngzhǎng, qiàqià shì jīfā zǔzhī nèibù chuàngxīn huólì yǔ jiānrèn rènxìng de guānjiàn suǒzài. | In crisis management, great leaders oversee strategy while calming troops with magnanimous equanimity during tactical errors. Allowing teams to learn from trial and error is the catalyst sparking innovation and resilient cohesion. | En la gestión de crisis, los líderes eminentes dominan el tablero estratégico y apaciguan ánimos con noble templanza ante los errores tácticos. Permitir aprender del ensayo y error es la clave que desata la creatividad y fortalece a los equipos.
